---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Editorial position, operating model, and inclusion criteria for streisandeffect.org.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the archive</p>
    <h1>Independent preservation with a clear point of view.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      streisandeffect.org is an independently operated personal archive. It is not affiliated with Amnesty International UK or any original publisher.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Editorial position</h2>
    <p>
      The archive operator is pro-trans and opposed to anti-trans political organizing. The archive does not pretend to be ideologically neutral, but factual claims, provenance claims, publisher statements, external criticism, and archive analysis are kept visibly separate.
    </p>
    <p>
      Documents are selected by the human operator. Hosting a document preserves a record for scrutiny; it does not automatically endorse every claim, framing, or conclusion inside that document.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section grid" aria-labelledby="criteria-heading">
    <h2 id="criteria-heading" class="screen-reader-only">Inclusion criteria</h2>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Public-interest value</h3>
      <p>The document helps accountability, research, criticism, or historical memory.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Institutional significance</h3>
      <p>The publisher, subject, removal, or dispute has institutional or political significance.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Verifiable provenance</h3>
      <p>The archive can identify the source, copy history, file metadata, and remaining uncertainty.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Documented removal or change</h3>
      <p>The record has been withdrawn, removed, materially changed, or made difficult to access.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Adequate context</h3>
      <p>The page can explain the document without collapsing fact, criticism, and archive opinion together.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Acceptable risk</h3>
      <p>Privacy, safety, legal, and provider-policy risks are weighed before publication.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Exclusions</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>Private personal information or doxxing.</li>
      <li>Unlawfully obtained private material.</li>
      <li>Malware, exploit payloads, or active tracking files.</li>
      <li>Material whose publication would create a serious safety risk.</li>
      <li>Documents that cannot be authenticated sufficiently for public presentation.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections are welcomed. Metadata changes, material contextual changes, and file replacements are dated and recorded when safe. Files are not silently replaced; replacement files receive new hashes and version information.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
